;; ---
;; --- Install the vendored bashbricks library.
;; ---
;; Until the `modernisation-world-bridge' work-stream, bashbricks was a
;; development-time dependency only: nothing that shipped ever sourced it.
;; bin/scripts/marionnet-natbridge.sh does, and it runs on the user's machine --
;; so the library has to be installed too.
;;
;; It goes into the scripts/ subdirectory of the share section, i.e. exactly
;; where marionnet-sudoers.sh, marionnet_telnet.sh and marionnet-natbridge.sh
;; land (bin/dune § install), which for an ordinary install means
;;   /usr/local/share/marionnet/scripts/
;; Keeping the four together is what makes the runtime probe of
;; marionnet-natbridge.sh trivial: the library is simply its neighbour.
;;
;; Consequence to be aware of: the Makefile mirrors ALL of
;; share/marionnet/scripts/* into $PREFIX/bin/ (hard links for
;; `install-final-as-root', symlinks for `install-for-testing'), so
;; bashbricks.sh is mirrored there as well, although it is a library to be
;; sourced rather than a command. Harmless, and it makes the probe work from
;; both directories.
;;
;; The `(source as destination)' form is the one already used by i18n/dune for
;; the gettext catalogues.
;; ---
(install
  (files (bashbricks.sh as scripts/bashbricks.sh))
  (section share)
  (package marionnet))
